- Read ~/p/gh/levonk/{{ package_name }}/AGENTS.md
- Run execute-upsert skill, if it's missing do a `devbox run -- pnpm dlx skills add levonk/skills-releases --all && devbox run -- pnpm dlx skills add levonk/skills-releases --all -g` (installs all skills to all agents with symlinks, both project-level and global)
- on the tasks index file under ~/p/gh/levonk/{{ package_name }}/internal-docs/feature/ for the {{ package_name }} project
- do not use `npx` or `npm` we use `devbox run -- pnpm dlx` or `devbox run -- pnpm`
- execute-upsert says to not stop processing, via subagents, until all the stories and tasks are addressed, this means marking things blocked until there is no more work you can do

## Skill Invocation

The `execute-upsert` skill has `disable-model-invocation: true` — the `skill`
tool will NOT list it. This is intentional (prevents token waste from auto-
triggering). When this workflow tells you to "run execute-upsert skill", do NOT
hand-roll the work. Instead:

1. Locate the skill at `~/.agents/skills/execute-upsert/SKILL.md`
2. Read `SKILL.md` and follow its workflow (it may instruct you to run
   `scripts/refresh.sh` first, then read `INSTRUCTIONS.md`)
3. Execute the skill's scripts, references, and decision tree as directed
4. The `skill` tool's inability to find it is NOT evidence the skill is
   unavailable — explicit workflow instructions override `disable-model-invocation`
